by Amoifr at 2026-04-07T06:24:18Z

Thanks @GromNaN for the detailed review and the optimization suggestions! 🙏

I've applied the PCRE optimization and fixed the comment. Here are the benchmark results:

### Helper::width() micro-benchmark (10,000 iterations)
| Input type | Before (µs) | After (µs) |
|------------|-------------|------------|
| ASCII string | 0.098 | 0.094 |
| Unicode string | 20.367 | 20.149 |
| Control chars | 2.829 | 2.920 |

### Table rendering benchmark
| Scenario | Before (ms/iter) | After (ms/iter) |
|----------|------------------|-----------------|
| Simple table (4 rows) | 0.0687 | 0.0628 |
| Large table (100 rows) | 1.159 | 1.085 |
| Colspan table | 0.0752 | 0.0695 |

The PCRE optimization is elegant but the gain is within statistical noise - the main benefit is cleaner code by avoiding the redundant UTF-8 validity check.

Regarding the colspan split optimization: I tried implementing the "skip when content fits" approach, but it broke some edge cases in the test suite. The interaction between `maxColumnWidths` initialization and the iterative width calculation made it tricky to get right without a more significant refactor. Happy to revisit if you have specific guidance on how to approach it!
